#
# Conformance case: cognition/calibration-forecast-series
# AC (ME12, design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md §Calibration assessment names an explicit series):
# a calibration assessment names an explicit forecast/outcome series with a scoring
# rule and reference class, kept APART from a single confidence value.
#
# Rule ex:isSeriesCalibration fires ONLY when a CognitiveAssessment is dimensioned
# on logic:dimensionCalibration AND names BOTH logic:assessmentEvidence (the series)
# AND logic:assessmentMethod (the scoring rule), where the series further names a
# reference class. The head carries the SERIES, so the derived fact records which
# forecast series the calibration is over — the series-side facts are surfaced, not
# merely bound and discarded.
#
# The negative control confAssess IS a calibration-dimensioned assessment carrying
# a logic:confidence value, but no series, scoring rule, or reference class. It must
# NOT satisfy the rule — proving the series-based framing is genuinely distinct from
# a single numeric confidence expression, even on a calibration assessment.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/cognition/calibration-forecast-series/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

ex:ruleIsSeriesCalibration a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleIsSeriesCalibration ;
    logic:head [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate ex:isSeriesCalibration ; rdf:object "?series" ] ;
    logic:body [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ; rdf:object logic:dimensionCalibration ] ,
               [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentEvidence ; rdf:object "?series" ] ,
               [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentMethod ; rdf:object "?rule" ] ,
               [ rdf:subject "?series" ; rdf:predicate ex:hasReferenceClass ; rdf:object "?refClass" ] .
